    "created_at": "2025-05-05T17:44:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-05T17:44:34Z",
    "body": "well opening a tab in background, there isnt a general api for that, i know thats because would be a severe security breach, \n\nBut still on browsers without extension support you want to open tabs in background like when browsing site or blog with multiple external links need to open them while still staying on same tab,\n\nonly way is to \nwindow.open(url);window.open().close()\nthat will open tab and bring back original tab, \nBut that had to be in single call so browsers block it as it was considered popup as two tabs being opened programatically\n\nNow when sites were given popup permission then it works\n\nBut when isnt it will open first tab, dont open second -> you have manually go to original tab -> allow popup -> now this opens the second tab but handler/reference would be null so we have to close it manually return to original tab -> now it works normall as popup are allowed\n\n\nThere isnt a 1) api to check if popup permission granted 2) there isnt a standard way to explicitely prompt trigger the popup permission toast for user to allow\n\nOnly trickery is to open two windows in single call window.open().close; window.open().close() , to trigger promt\n\nBut browsers keep accumulating urls when multiple such calls made and permissions not given, when allowev all opened at once with no handler to close\n\n\nMaybe this was wrong place to post, maybe it was browser devs to be asked,\nor on some javascript related place, but dont know any such so i asked here",
